---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Penguin-Layout.astro';
import Navbar from '../../components/Navbar.astro';

const currentDate = new Date();
let currentYear = currentDate.getFullYear();
---

<Layout title="Penguins">
    <head>
        <meta charset="UTF-8">
        <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
        <title>Royal Penguin</title>
    </head>
    <body>
        <header class="header">
            <h1>Royal Penguin</h1>
        </header>
        <Navbar/>
        <main>
            <div class="container">
                <nav class="contents">
                    <h2>Contents:</h2>
                    <ul>
                        <li><a href="#overview">Overview</a></li>
                        <li><a href="#diet">Diet</a></li>
                        <li><a href="#behavior">Social Behavior</a></li>
                        <li><a href="#facts">Facts</a></li>
                    </ul>
                </nav>

                <section id="overview">
                    <h2>Overview</h2>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Scientific Name: Eudyptes schlegeli</li>
                        <li>Size: Approximately 65-75 cm (26-30 inches) tall, weighing 3-6 kg (6.6-13.2 lbs).</li>
                        <li>Habitat: Breeds almost exclusively on Macquarie Island and its surrounding Bishop and Clerk Islands, located in the subantarctic region. They disperse into the Southern Ocean during the non-breeding season.</li>
                        <li>Conservation Status: Vulnerable</li>
                    </ul>
                </section>
                <section id="diet">
                    <h2>Diet</h2>
                    <p>The Royal Penguin's diet consists mainly of krill, as well as some small fish and squid, which they forage for in the nutrient-rich waters around Macquarie Island.</p>
                </section>
                <section id="behavior">
                    <h2>Social Behavior</h2>
                    <p>Royal Penguins breed in large, dense colonies on the coastal slopes of Macquarie Island. They are social birds with loud vocalizations and displays during the breeding season to establish territories and pair bonds. They form monogamous pairs and both parents participate in incubating the eggs and raising the chicks.</p>
                </section>
                <section id="facts">
                    <h2>Interesting Facts</h2>
                    <ul>
                        <li>They have a distinctive pale yellow to white crest that extends along the sides of their head.</li>
                        <li>Royal Penguins are often considered a subspecies of the Macaroni Penguin due to their similar appearance and genetics.</li>
                        <li>Their breeding colonies can be very large, sometimes covering extensive areas of the island.</li>
                        <li>Macquarie Island is a World Heritage Site and a crucial breeding ground for Royal Penguins.</li>
                        <li>Populations have experienced fluctuations, and conservation efforts are important to ensure their long-term survival.</li>
                    </ul>
                </section>
            </div>
            <footer>
                <p><span class="copyleft">&copy;</span> PengiCoder & MrPiggy105, { currentYear }</p>
            </footer>
        </main>
    </body>
</Layout>

<style>
    .contents ul {
        list-style-type: none;
        padding: 0;
    }

    .contents li {
        margin-bottom: 10px;
    }

    section {
        overflow: hidden;
        margin-bottom: 20px;
        margin-left: 30%;
    }

    h1{
        text-align: center;
        height: 100%;
        font-family: 'Orkney', Arial;
    }
</style>